kind: scene
id: chapter-two
title: The Glass Stair
on: chapter
after: 'visited("chapter-one")'
---

## The Glass Stair

::bg{location="lighthouse" time="noon"}
::music{playback="change" mood="tense" volume="loud" assetId="music.tense"}
::actor{character="mara" anchor="center" action="fadeIn" emotion="worried" costume="raincloak"}
::actor{character="elio" anchor="right" action="fadeIn" emotion="surprised" costume="coat"}
::camera{focus="mara" framing="close" transition="wipeLeft"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The lighthouse door opens onto a stair made of glass. Below it, the sea is much too near.
@elio{code="0010" emotion="surprised"}: The stairs are humming.
@mara{code="0010" emotion="worried"}: They remember every footstep.
<match subject="run.choice">
  <when is="tower">
    @mara{code="0020" emotion="hopeful"}: We chose the high road. Now we finish it.
  </when>
  <when is="harbor">
    @elio{code="0020" emotion="happy"}: You chose the long way around, and somehow it led here.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator{code="0020"}: You cannot remember choosing a road, only that it is behind you.
  </otherwise>
</match>
<branch id="crossing" prompt="A bell rings above the stair. The next step is already fading." timeout="8" default="steady">
  <choice id="steady" text="Cross together">
    ::set{run.trust += 1}
    @mara{code="0030" emotion="hopeful"}: Hand in hand. No vanishing alone.
  </choice>
  <choice id="rush" text="Run for the lantern">
    ::set{run.trust -= 1}
    @elio{code="0030" emotion="worried"}: Mara, wait!
  </choice>
</branch>
::cg{assetId="cg.lighthouse" display="show" layout="full"}
@narrator{code="0030"}: Behind the lantern, a figure turns toward you. It has Mara's eyes.
::cg{assetId="cg.lighthouse" display="hide"}
::sfx{sound="glass" assetId="sfx.glass"}
::vfx{type="shake" transition="wipeLeft"}
::actor{character="mara" emotion="angry" action="shake"}
@mara{code="0040" emotion="angry"}: My sister. She is still here.
@mara{code="0050" emotion="worried"}: The glass was made from sand taken beneath the harbor.
@elio{code="0040" emotion="neutral"}: So the lighthouse is standing on our secrets.
@mara{code="0060" emotion="sad"}: Every town builds on something it refuses to remember.
@elio{code="0050" emotion="happy"}: I refuse to remember the price of this umbrella.
@mara{code="0070" emotion="happy"}: It has holes.
@elio{code="0060" emotion="surprised"}: Character, not holes.
@narrator{code="0040"}: Above, the lantern pulses with a patient blue light.
@mara{code="0080" emotion="hopeful"}: Liora is calling through the lens.
@elio{code="0070" emotion="worried"}: Then call back.
@mara{code="0090" emotion="neutral"}: I am afraid she will answer.
@elio{code="0080" emotion="hopeful"}: Fear is an answer too. It means we care where the road ends.
@narrator{code="0050"}: Their footsteps ring out, each one a small promise.
@mara{code="0100" emotion="sad"}: I should have followed her three years ago.
@elio{code="0090" emotion="angry"}: You were sixteen.
@mara{code="0110" emotion="worried"}: Old enough to say goodbye.
@elio{code="0100" emotion="happy"}: Nobody says goodbye correctly the first time.
@mara{code="0120" emotion="hopeful"}: You make that sound like experience.
@elio{code="0110" emotion="sad"}: My brother left on a fishing boat. I kept the kettle warm for a month.
@narrator{code="0060"}: The stair bends toward a locked door.
@mara{code="0130" emotion="surprised"}: The blue ribbon is tied to the handle.
@elio{code="0120" emotion="neutral"}: Then we open it together.
@mara{code="0140" emotion="hopeful"}: Together.
<branch id="doorMemory" prompt="The locked door shows three memories.">
  <choice id="remember" text="Remember Liora's laugh">
    ::set{run.heardSignal = true}
    @mara{code="0150" emotion="happy"}: I can still hear her.
  </choice>
</branch>
